WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.924 --> 00:00:11.084
Mother's friend Mrs.

2
00:00:11.204 --> 00:00:16.466
Kirke sent a telegram asking Jo to come right away, saying her room was ready and waiting for

3
00:00:16.526 --> 00:00:21.728
her. Now it was time for Jo to spread her wings and fly just like the birds she

4
00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:23.229
had always envied and admired.

5
00:00:23.909 --> 00:00:26.970
But having to explain that to Beth was harder than she thought.

6
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.752
"What if I never see you again?"

7
00:00:30.072 --> 00:00:30.672
cried Beth.

8
00:00:31.556 --> 00:00:35.497
"I'm coming back after the winter, Beth," Jo comforted her sister.

9
00:00:35.517 --> 00:00:41.779
"I'm sorry if I sound selfish, but I can't bear it if you leave too," said Beth.

10
00:00:42.679 --> 00:00:48.221
After Jo had made many more reassurances and promises, Beth finally gave in and wished her the best

11
00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.382
of luck with this new chapter in her life.

12
00:00:52.582 --> 00:00:57.224
Upstairs in her sanctuary, Jo collected her writing materials and her writer's smock.

13
00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:03.422
She intended to complete her novel during her "expedition," as she called it, since each day would be

14
00:01:03.582 --> 00:01:04.203
an adventure.

15
00:01:04.923 --> 00:01:08.444
Within a few days, Jo was packed and ready to depart for New York City.

16
00:01:09.385 --> 00:01:12.406
Her family and friends waited downstairs to say good-bye to her.

17
00:01:12.426 --> 00:01:19.489
"Jo, be careful because John says New York is a very dangerous place, so you ought to walk

18
00:01:19.549 --> 00:01:25.291
with your head up and alert, never go out alone, and always carry an umbrella," warned Meg.

19
00:01:25.311 --> 00:01:26.792
"An umbrella?

20
00:01:27.144 --> 00:01:27.724
For what?"

21
00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:28.724
laughed Father.

22
00:01:28.744 --> 00:01:33.946
"For protection, just in case, you know as a weapon," Meg stammered.

23
00:01:33.966 --> 00:01:39.867
"We're very proud of you, darling, and we want you to have lots of adventures, but we are

24
00:01:39.927 --> 00:01:42.568
counting the days till you return," said Mother.

25
00:01:43.348 --> 00:01:44.549
Beth didn't say anything.

26
00:01:45.069 --> 00:01:47.169
She just hugged Jo tightly for a long time.

27
00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:54.091
"I'll carry your bags to the carriage," Laurie said, picking up the light luggage before Jo could protest.

28
00:01:56.112 --> 00:02:01.074
Outside, Laurie waited for her while she said her final farewells to her family.

29
00:02:02.075 --> 00:02:06.477
Then when she approached, he burst out, "You're not planning on returning, are you?"

30
00:02:06.497 --> 00:02:09.018
"Don't make a scene, Laurie.

31
00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:13.721
Of course I'm coming back," Jo said, glancing back to see if Beth was watching them.

32
00:02:13.741 --> 00:02:20.284
"Well, I'll let you go this time, Jo March, but if for some crazy reason you decide to

33
00:02:20.324 --> 00:02:23.626
stay in New York, I'm coming to get you," Laurie threatened.

34
00:02:24.407 --> 00:02:29.377
Hugging her dearest friend, Jo whispered in his ear, "Look after sweet Beth, will you?

35
00:02:29.797 --> 00:02:30.857
You're all she has now."

36
00:02:30.877 --> 00:02:32.378
"I will, Jo.

37
00:02:32.978 --> 00:02:34.758
I'll look after her," promised Laurie.

38
00:02:35.979 --> 00:02:39.900
Jo stepped up into the carriage and soon she was on her way to New York.

39
00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:47.362
Meanwhile, many exciting events were unfolding in the life of Amy March, as she continued her tour of

40
00:02:47.462 --> 00:02:53.224
Europe. Aunt March had rented a beautiful villa in Nice, France, where the scenery was breathtaking.

41
00:02:54.384 --> 00:02:59.946
Every morning, Amy had to pinch herself as a reminder that she wasn't dreaming but was truly in

42
00:02:59.986 --> 00:03:01.826
the most romantic country in the world.

43
00:03:02.786 --> 00:03:08.188
While Aunt March napped in the afternoon, Amy went out by herself, carrying just a sketchbook and her

44
00:03:08.228 --> 00:03:11.329
parasol, which no European girl left home without.

45
00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:16.050
She would wander along the beach until she found a spot that she wanted to draw.

46
00:03:17.971 --> 00:03:21.672
With so many beautiful scenes everywhere, her sketchbook was soon filled.

47
00:03:23.256 --> 00:03:29.199
One particular afternoon while Amy was drawing a little girl playing in the ocean, a well-dressed young man

48
00:03:29.339 --> 00:03:30.359
carefully approached her.

49
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.241
Speaking in French, he asked, "May I see what's making you smile so much?"

50
00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:41.544
During the short time she had been in Europe, Amy had already learned a few expressions in French,

51
00:03:41.684 --> 00:03:42.744
German, and Italian.

52
00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:48.086
So she fluently answered the young man's question and showed him her drawing.

53
00:03:49.127 --> 00:03:54.465
He made all sorts of lovely compliments in rapid French that Amy didn't understand, but she nodded and

54
00:03:54.545 --> 00:03:55.686
smiled as if she did.

55
00:03:55.706 --> 00:04:00.948
"I'm sorry," Amy finally admitted when she could no longer fake it.

56
00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.069
"My French is very limited."

57
00:04:03.089 --> 00:04:05.250
"Oh! You're American!

58
00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.331
So am I!"

59
00:04:06.611 --> 00:04:07.631
the young man exclaimed.

60
00:04:07.651 --> 00:04:08.692
"I'm Fred.

61
00:04:09.052 --> 00:04:09.752
What's your name?"

62
00:04:10.592 --> 00:04:15.195
Amy introduced herself, and soon the two of them were having a lively conversation.

63
00:04:16.635 --> 00:04:23.119
Across the Atlantic Ocean, Jo had just arrived in New York City after an exceptionally tiring but fascinating

64
00:04:23.179 --> 00:04:27.742
journey, during which she'd discovered landscapes that she had never seen before.

65
00:04:27.762 --> 00:04:30.324
"Oh, my gracious me!"

66
00:04:30.644 --> 00:04:33.586
Jo gasped as she gazed around at her surroundings.

67
00:04:34.566 --> 00:04:40.790
Nothing could prepare her for the experience of New York City, where swarms of people bustled about on

68
00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:43.472
busy streets lined with building after building.

69
00:04:44.576 --> 00:04:50.578
Jo felt dizzy with excitement just thinking about the opportunities before her to explore all that the city

70
00:04:50.638 --> 00:04:51.338
had to offer.

71
00:04:51.978 --> 00:04:56.500
Mrs. Kirke's home was on a quiet street with large trees planted in a row in front of

72
00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.800
each house.

73
00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.721
"Jo! Welcome to New York!"

74
00:05:01.021 --> 00:05:04.702
Mrs. Kirke called out happily when she opened the door to let Jo in.

75
00:05:05.502 --> 00:05:11.904
Mrs. Kirke was a few years younger than Mother, but had the same warm, inviting smile, which instantly

76
00:05:11.964 --> 00:05:14.845
reminded Jo how much she already missed her family.

77
00:05:14.865 --> 00:05:20.647
"The girls are at the park now and will be home in a few minutes, so I'll show

78
00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.608
you around the house," Mrs.

79
00:05:22.668 --> 00:05:24.729
Kirke said, taking one of Jo's suitcases.

80
00:05:25.769 --> 00:05:28.390
Everything in the house was well organized and clean.

81
00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:33.832
Once Jo saw her room, she knew her stay at the Kirkes' home would be a pleasant one.

82
00:05:35.016 --> 00:05:40.838
Located on the top floor of the house, Jo's room had one large window that boasted a fabulous

83
00:05:40.898 --> 00:05:42.359
view of the city in the distance.

84
00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:47.861
In front of the window was a large oak desk, where Jo could work on her novel and

85
00:05:47.881 --> 00:05:49.462
look outside whenever she wanted.

86
00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:54.584
Just standing there inspired Jo to pull out her paper and start writing immediately.

87
00:05:54.604 --> 00:05:58.046
"I hope you are happy here, Jo," Mrs.

88
00:05:58.086 --> 00:05:58.766
Kirke was saying.

89
00:05:58.786 --> 00:06:01.887
"We want you to feel as if this is your home."

90
00:06:01.907 --> 00:06:03.368
"Thank you, Mrs.

91
00:06:04.148 --> 00:06:05.168
Kirke," Jo said gratefully.

92
00:06:05.188 --> 00:06:07.329
"I am already falling in love with it."

93
00:06:08.269 --> 00:06:10.810
"Oh, before I forget," added Mrs.

94
00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.011
Kirke. "We have a tenant who rents the floor beneath you.

95
00:06:15.011 --> 00:06:16.332
I'll introduce you later.

96
00:06:16.912 --> 00:06:19.993
His name is Friedrich Bauer but we call him Professor.

97
00:06:21.593 --> 00:06:23.434
Oh, I hear the girls returning.

98
00:06:23.774 --> 00:06:25.374
Would you like to meet them now, Jo?"

99
00:06:25.394 --> 00:06:29.075
"Yes, I would," said Jo, following her downstairs.

100
00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:35.197
Back at the March home, Laurie was keeping his promise to Jo by making sure that Beth did

101
00:06:35.237 --> 00:06:36.217
not get too lonely.

102
00:06:36.957 --> 00:06:41.099
They sat for a few hours while Beth played the piano and they laughed as they chatted about

103
00:06:41.179 --> 00:06:41.759
old times.

104
00:06:41.779 --> 00:06:45.960
"I'm going back to school in two days, Beth," Laurie told her.

105
00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:49.081
"Will you be okay without your sisters and me around?"

106
00:06:49.681 --> 00:06:52.302
Smiling, Beth reassured him that she would be fine.

107
00:06:52.322 --> 00:06:55.903
"I have Meg, Mother, Father, Mr.

108
00:06:55.963 --> 00:07:00.744
Laurence, and of course, my beloved piano to occupy my days," she said.

109
00:07:01.784 --> 00:07:04.205
"Do you think Jo will come back a different person?"

110
00:07:04.585 --> 00:07:05.705
Laurie asked cautiously.

111
00:07:06.565 --> 00:07:12.927
Beth thought for a moment then replied rather sadly, "Yes, but change is inevitable.

112
00:07:13.768 --> 00:07:17.709
We must all face the truth and accept that nothing can stay the same forever."

113
00:07:17.729 --> 00:07:22.570
"I don't want things to ever change," Laurie said childishly.

114
00:07:23.211 --> 00:07:27.592
Neither one of them, however, could have predicted how much their lives were going to be transformed.
